{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "The Rust stack's pinned toolchain archives (manifest.ts reads them as RUST_MANIFEST). Every URL is a durable release URL on its component's release host (RELEASE_URL_PREFIXES); each sha256 is the one scripts/spike/rust-wgpu/pins.md records from the official source's published checksum, each size the downloaded archive's (darwin-arm64) or the release host's Content-Length (linux-x64, 2026-10-06). The crate checker (cargo-deny, cargo-vet and the RustSec snapshot `crate-policy.json` pins; `scripts/toolchains/crate-policy.ts refresh` moves the snapshot) installs on demand at the person's first crate approval and is in no build lock. The vendored crate set (rust-vendor) joins once the owner publishes a `genex` release cut by `scripts/toolchains/rust-release.ts cut` and `rust-release.ts pin` adds it. libcolyseus (colyseus, colyseus-source; MP-1a) is pinned by the GitHub release digest of each Colyseus native-sdk v0.18.10 asset, checked against the downloaded bytes on 2026-10-20; only an export of a `[net]` game installs it (`RUST_NET_COMPONENTS`). Android's libcolyseus is built from the source (colyseus-source, MP-1b, owner decision G12) with zig 0.15.2 (upstream's build.zig refuses any other zig; ziglang.org's download/index.json digest, checked against the downloaded bytes) and the zig_msgpack archive build.zig.zon names (commit 47c15d2, sha256 taken on download, its zig package hash checked with zig fetch), one entry per host. The browser's relay bridge (genex-mp-bridge, MP-5a) is @genex-ai/multiplayer 0.17.0's npm tarball, its sha256 taken on download on 2026-10-21 after its sha512 matched the registry's published integrity; only a web export of a `[net]` game installs it.",
